    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37267" root="كنبث" body-key="k">
    
      Q. 1 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كَنْبَثَ</span></b>  and ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَكَنْبَثَ</span></b>  <i>He became hard and
strong:</i> (L:) <i>he became contracted;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَقَبَّضَ</span>:
(K:) [app. <i>in disposition;</i> see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">كُنْبُثٌ</span>: or <i>in
make;</i> the second verb being also expl. in the L,
with reference to a man, by the words <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تَدَاخَلَ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَعْضُهُ فِى بَعْضٍ</span>].

